{% doc %}
  Main navigation list (DESIGN.md §6.1, DS-11, DS-133). Rendered twice by gs-header: once for the
  Menu drawer and once for the desktop bar.

  Model: a top-level item is either a plain link (no children) or one button that opens its
  dropdown (has children). The button is the <summary> of a <details>, so it works without
  JavaScript and never navigates. The section's main page must be one of the dropdown's links,
  normally the first, with its own label (e.g. "About the gallery"). The bar's dropdowns share a
  name, so opening one closes the others; the drawer's sections open independently, in place, so a
  tapped row never jumps away (DS-104).

  Groups (DS-133): an item in a dropdown that has items of its own is a group. Its title links to
  its own page ("Artists for Kids"), or is plain text when its link is "#" ("Scholarships and
  awards"), and its items are listed under it. On the bar the groups sit side by side, one column
  each, in a panel that ends at the nav's right edge; in the drawer they stack. Items without items
  of their own run across the top. Nothing opens inside a dropdown: the menu editor's third level
  draws the groups, and it has no fourth.

  Enforced here, because the menu editor can't enforce it:
  - A parent whose link points to a page that isn't in its dropdown (an item, a group's title or a
    group's item) gets a theme-editor warning: visitors could no longer reach that page from the
    menu. Fix by adding the page to the dropdown, or set the parent's link to "#" if no main page is
    intended.
  - An item or group labelled exactly like its section gets a warning: give it its own label.
  - Store URLs typed as absolute links are made relative; true off-site links get the
    external cue and "(external site)" for screen readers (gs-url).
  - A plain link with no destination ("#") gets a warning.
  - The current section's button or link says ", current section" to screen readers (a plain link
    only when the page isn't its own); in the drawer its dropdown starts open, so people see where
    they are. A group's item counts, as a dropdown's item does.
  - Section names longer than 73 characters together, or more than seven sections, get a
    warning: the bar has little to spare on one line at 1200 px.
  - A page the menu can't list belongs to a section through the pages in Theme settings (DS-91,
    DS-134): an artist's, work's or grouping's page marks the section that links to the Permanent
    Collection or Artists page; an exhibition, and the Upcoming and Past pages, mark the one that
    links to an exhibitions page; a limited edition, portfolio or the collections list marks the one
    that links to the Shop page. A section's own link counts, so a plain link (Exhibitions to On now,
    Shop) is marked too. Only when no menu link is active, and at most one section.
  - A page or lesson the menu doesn't list counts as inside the section whose main page (its own
    link, its first item or a group's title) belongs to the same programme: After School Art or a
    lesson marks the section with the Artists for Kids group. At most one section; exhibition and
    event pages never trigger it.

  @param {object} menu - A menu (linklist), e.g. section.settings.menu
  @param {string} [brand] - The page's programme as a brand scope (gs-brand), from gs-header
  @param {string} [variant] - 'bar' (default) or 'drawer'. Editor warnings show once, with the bar

  @example
  {%- render 'gs-nav', menu: menu, variant: 'drawer' -%}
{% enddoc %}
{%- liquid
  assign variant = variant | default: 'bar'
  # The section a page belongs to when the menu can't list it (DS-91, DS-134): its anchor pages.
  assign exhibition_list = false
  if page.id != blank
    if page.id == settings.exhibitions_upcoming_page.id or page.id == settings.exhibitions_past_page.id
      assign exhibition_list = true
    endif
  endif
  assign anchors = ''
  if request.path contains '/pages/artists/' or request.path contains '/pages/collection/' or request.path contains '/pages/browse/'
    assign anchors = settings.collection_page.url | append: '|' | append: settings.artists_page.url
  elsif request.path contains '/pages/exhibitions/' or exhibition_list
    assign anchors = settings.exhibitions_on_now_page.url | append: '|' | append: settings.exhibitions_upcoming_page.url | append: '|' | append: settings.exhibitions_past_page.url
  elsif request.page_type == 'product' or request.page_type == 'collection' or request.page_type == 'list-collections'
    assign anchors = settings.shop_page.url
  endif
  assign anchors = anchors | split: '|'
  assign anchor_marked = false

  # Whether the menu lists this page, at any of its three levels.
  assign listed = false
  for l in menu.links
    if l.active or l.child_active
      assign listed = true
    else
      for c in l.links
        for g in c.links
          if g.active
            assign listed = true
          endif
        endfor
      endfor
    endif
    if listed
      break
    endif
  endfor

  assign find_programme = false
  if listed == false and anchors.size == 0 and brand != blank and brand != 'gallery'
    if template.name == 'page' or metaobject.system.type == 'lesson'
      assign find_programme = true
    endif
  endif
  assign programme_marked = false
-%}
<ul class="gs-nav">
  {%- for link in menu.links -%}
    {%- capture r -%}{%- render 'gs-url', link: link -%}{%- endcapture -%}
    {%- assign r = r | strip | split: '|' -%}
    {%- assign href = r[0] -%}
    {%- assign ext = r[1] -%}
    {%- assign title = link.title | strip | escape -%}
    {%- assign title_key = link.title | strip | downcase -%}
    {%- liquid
      assign is_current = false
      if link.active or link.child_active
        assign is_current = true
      endif
      assign groups = 0
      for child in link.links
        if child.links.size > 0
          assign groups = groups | plus: 1
          for grandchild in child.links
            if grandchild.active
              assign is_current = true
            endif
          endfor
        endif
      endfor

      if listed == false and anchor_marked == false and anchors.size > 0
        if anchors contains link.url
          assign anchor_marked = true
        else
          for child in link.links
            if anchors contains child.url
              assign anchor_marked = true
            else
              for grandchild in child.links
                if anchors contains grandchild.url
                  assign anchor_marked = true
                endif
              endfor
            endif
            if anchor_marked
              break
            endif
          endfor
        endif
        if anchor_marked
          assign is_current = true
        endif
      endif

      # The section's main pages: its own link, its first item and its groups' titles.
      if find_programme and programme_marked == false and link.links.size > 0
        assign candidates = ''
        if link.type == 'page_link'
          capture b
            render 'gs-programme', value: link.object.metafields.custom.programme.value
          endcapture
          assign candidates = candidates | append: b | append: ','
        endif
        if link.links.first.type == 'page_link'
          capture b
            render 'gs-programme', value: link.links.first.object.metafields.custom.programme.value
          endcapture
          assign candidates = candidates | append: b | append: ','
        endif
        for child in link.links
          if child.links.size > 0 and child.type == 'page_link'
            capture b
              render 'gs-programme', value: child.object.metafields.custom.programme.value
            endcapture
            assign candidates = candidates | append: b | append: ','
          endif
        endfor
        assign candidates = candidates | strip_newlines | remove: ' ' | split: ','
        if candidates contains brand
          assign is_current = true
          assign programme_marked = true
        endif
      endif
    -%}

    <li class="gs-nav__item{% if is_current %} gs-nav__item--current{% endif %}{% if groups > 0 %} gs-nav__item--groups{% endif %}">
      {%- if link.links.size > 0 -%}
        {%- assign parent_listed = false -%}
        {%- assign repeated_label = false -%}
        <details class="gs-nav__details"{% if variant == 'bar' %} name="gs-nav-bar"{% endif %}{% if variant == 'drawer' and is_current %} open{% endif %}>
          <summary class="gs-nav__trigger">
            {{- title -}}
            {%- if is_current -%}<span class="gs-visually-hidden">{{ 'header.current_section' | t }}</span>{%- endif -%}
          </summary>
          <ul class="gs-nav__panel{% if groups > 0 %} gs-nav__panel--groups{% endif %}"{% if groups > 0 %} style="--gs-nav-groups: {{ groups }}"{% endif %}>
            {%- for child in link.links -%}
              {%- capture c -%}{%- render 'gs-url', link: child -%}{%- endcapture -%}
              {%- assign c = c | strip | split: '|' -%}
              {%- if c[0] == href -%}{%- assign parent_listed = true -%}{%- endif -%}
              {%- assign child_key = child.title | strip | downcase -%}
              {%- if child_key == title_key -%}{%- assign repeated_label = true -%}{%- endif -%}
              {%- if child.links.size > 0 -%}
                {%- assign group_id = 'gs-nav-' | append: variant | append: '-' | append: forloop.parentloop.index | append: '-' | append: forloop.index -%}
                <li class="gs-nav__group">
                  {%- if c[0] == '#' -%}
                    <span class="gs-nav__group-title" id="{{ group_id }}">{{ child.title | strip | escape }}</span>
                  {%- else -%}
                    <a class="gs-nav__group-title{% if c[1] == '1' %} gs-link--external{% endif %}" id="{{ group_id }}" href="{{ c[0] }}"{% if child.current %} aria-current="page"{% endif %}>
                      {{- child.title | strip | escape -}}
                      {%- if c[1] == '1' -%}<span class="gs-visually-hidden"> {{ 'general.external_site' | t }}</span>{%- endif -%}
                    </a>
                  {%- endif -%}
                  <ul aria-labelledby="{{ group_id }}">
                    {%- for grandchild in child.links -%}
                      {%- capture g -%}{%- render 'gs-url', link: grandchild -%}{%- endcapture -%}
                      {%- assign g = g | strip | split: '|' -%}
                      {%- if g[0] == href -%}{%- assign parent_listed = true -%}{%- endif -%}
                      <li>
                        <a href="{{ g[0] }}"{% if grandchild.current %} aria-current="page"{% endif %}{% if g[1] == '1' %} class="gs-link--external"{% endif %}>
                          {{- grandchild.title | strip | escape -}}
                          {%- if g[1] == '1' -%}<span class="gs-visually-hidden"> {{ 'general.external_site' | t }}</span>{%- endif -%}
                        </a>
                      </li>
                    {%- endfor -%}
                  </ul>
                </li>
              {%- else -%}
                <li>
                  <a href="{{ c[0] }}"{% if child.current %} aria-current="page"{% endif %}{% if c[1] == '1' %} class="gs-link--external"{% endif %}>
                    {{- child.title | strip | escape -}}
                    {%- if c[1] == '1' -%}<span class="gs-visually-hidden"> {{ 'general.external_site' | t }}</span>{%- endif -%}
                  </a>
                </li>
              {%- endif -%}
            {%- endfor -%}
          </ul>
        </details>
        {%- if request.design_mode and variant == 'bar' -%}
          {%- if href != '#' and parent_listed == false -%}
            <span class="gs-editor-warning">"{{ title }}" links to {{ href }}, which isn't in its dropdown, so visitors can't reach it from the menu. Add it as the first item with its own label, or set this item's link to #.</span>
          {%- endif -%}
          {%- if repeated_label -%}
            <span class="gs-editor-warning">An item in the "{{ title }}" dropdown has the same label as the section. Give it its own label, e.g. "About {{ title }}".</span>
          {%- endif -%}
        {%- endif -%}
      {%- else -%}
        <a class="gs-nav__link{% if ext == '1' %} gs-link--external{% endif %}" href="{{ href }}"{% if link.current %} aria-current="page"{% endif %}>
          {{- title -}}
          {%- if ext == '1' -%}<span class="gs-visually-hidden"> {{ 'general.external_site' | t }}</span>{%- endif -%}
          {%- if is_current and link.current == false -%}<span class="gs-visually-hidden">{{ 'header.current_section' | t }}</span>{%- endif -%}
        </a>
        {%- if request.design_mode and variant == 'bar' and href == '#' -%}
          <span class="gs-editor-warning">Menu item "{{ title }}" has no page. Link it to a page or add items under it.</span>
        {%- endif -%}
      {%- endif -%}
    </li>
  {%- endfor -%}
  {%- if request.design_mode and variant == 'bar' -%}
    {%- assign name_chars = 0 -%}
    {%- for l in menu.links -%}
      {%- assign l_chars = l.title | strip | size -%}
      {%- assign name_chars = name_chars | plus: l_chars -%}
    {%- endfor -%}
    {%- if name_chars > 73 or menu.links.size > 7 -%}
      <li><span class="gs-editor-warning">The main menu's section names are too long to fit on one line on laptop screens. Shorten one, or ask for the layout to be checked.</span></li>
    {%- endif -%}
  {%- endif -%}
</ul>
